{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1054924-what-s-your-weird-food-related-habit","id":1054924,"title":"What's your weird food related habit?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-25T13:42:15-08:00","id":1054924,"title":"What's your weird food related habit?","content":"I'll start. I literally eat the salt off pretzels. Also, I chew ice. Into tiny pieces. And when I get a snow cone, it's just because I want the ice, so I don't get any flavoring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T13:45:53-08:00","id":1054926,"title":"","content":"I thankfully grew out of this, but as a child I lived for A1 steak sauce, to the point where I would use it instead of gravy on mashed potatos and would have steak sauce and bacon sandwiches to bring the school.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T13:53:16-08:00","id":1054928,"title":"","content":"Sometimes when I want something to munch on, I'll get some crushed ice and pour a tiny bit of salt on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T14:02:18-08:00","id":1054931,"title":"","content":"When I was a kid, I liked getting whole wheat bread, taking the inside off of the crust, rolling it into a ball to eat it. And I'd put ketchup on that ball.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T14:09:25-08:00","id":1054932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1054924-what-s-your-weird-food-related-habit?p=1054928#post1054928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sometimes when I want something to munch on, I'll get some crushed ice and pour a tiny bit of salt on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>We're clearly meant to be friends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T14:18:37-08:00","id":1054937,"title":"","content":"I always eat the edges of flat bread dishes (like sandwiches and pizzas) first, and I sometimes go in a spiral in towards the middle after that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 02-25-2017, 06:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T14:25:08-08:00","id":1054939,"title":"","content":"I do the ice chewing thing too. Crushed ice is best, but I'll do it with any ice I have.<br /> <br /> When I was younger I used to always eat meals one food at a time. Now I do pretty much the opposite and mix everything together.<br /> <br /> As a kid, my mom would always have the fridge stocked with pitted, pemento-stuffed green olives. The olives were too sour for me, but I loved the pimentos, so I would take olives right out of the jar, suck the pimentos out, and throw away the actual olives.<br /> <br /> When I eat chicken wings I pick the bones <i>clean</i>. Even eat the gristle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T14:34:54-08:00","id":1054943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1054924-what-s-your-weird-food-related-habit?p=1054939#post1054939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I eat chicken wings I pick the bones <i>clean</i>. Even eat the gristle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also me.<br /> <br /> And shrimp tails...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T14:37:21-08:00","id":1054944,"title":"","content":"I rarely reheat left overs, just eat it cold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T14:56:37-08:00","id":1054950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1054924-what-s-your-weird-food-related-habit?p=1054939#post1054939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I eat chicken wings I pick the bones <i>clean</i>. Even eat the gristle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you even crack open the bones and suck out the marrow? I have a friend who always do that. I've never enjoyed marrow enough to do it very often, myself though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T14:58:28-08:00","id":1054952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1054924-what-s-your-weird-food-related-habit?p=1054950#post1054950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you even crack open the bones and suck out the marrow? I have a friend who always do that. I've never enjoyed marrow enough to do it very often, myself though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've tried it, but I don't really like the texture of the marrow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T15:03:06-08:00","id":1054954,"title":"","content":"When I was a kid... I'd only eat foods in the orange-yellow-brown spectrum, to the point my mother conceded to buying the quick mac n cheese stuff so she could use the artificial orange food coloring dye to add it to her from-scratch mac n cheese; since it was too white.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T15:40:26-08:00","id":1054966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1054924-what-s-your-weird-food-related-habit?p=1054939#post1054939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do the ice chewing thing too. Crushed ice is best, but I'll do it with any ice I have.<br /> <br /> When I was younger I used to always eat meals one food at a time. Now I do pretty much the opposite and mix everything together.<br /> <br /> As a kid, my mom would always have the fridge stocked with pitted, pemento-stuffed green olives. The olives were too sour for me, but I loved the pimentos, so I would take olives right out of the jar, suck the pimentos out, and throw away the actual olives.<br /> <br /> When I eat chicken wings I pick the bones <i>clean</i>. Even eat the gristle.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're talking to the gal who used to suck up and spit out the pimento because she hated it, then would go to town on the now-empty olives and maybe have a sip or two of brine.<br /> <br /> Now I just get them stuffed with garlic instead, and have mostly done away with brine-drinking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T15:49:35-08:00","id":1054969,"title":"","content":"I like to burn cheese until it's gets really dark to eat it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T15:57:34-08:00","id":1054972,"title":"","content":"weird food habits? well...<br /> <br /> I sometimes eat pure sugar. I mean, I sometimes just take a spoon of sugar and eat it. If I'm at a cafe, I may take a small bag of sugar, crush it for ten minutes or so and then eat it. I also need to &quot;engineer my burger&quot;, as my friends like to say- it means I waste around 20 minutes (sometimes more) to put the layers chips, sauces and any other kind of extras on my burger at certain order and at certain shape. I also can't eat any kind of meat unless it is Well Done. I just can't make myself swallow it (it means I can't eat sushi or smoked meat). Talking about order in food, I have to eat my dishes at certain order- for example, I'll never eat my burger before finishing all of my chips, or that I'll always eat the fried mushrooms before I'll eat my fish (I eat mushrooms with almost anything- and I add soy sauce to almost everything. That's also count, right?). When I was a child, I had even more, worse habits (for example, now I almost never eat sugar, and when I was a child I couldn't even start eating the chips before finish drinking my coke.)<br /> <br /> But other than that- no, no strange food habits at all :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T16:00:11-08:00","id":1054974,"title":"","content":"I used to add dill pickle slices to my pepperoni pizza when I was a kid. I liked sour cream on my French Fries. Nowadays, I still won't touch anything with mushrooms, and I think people who put mayonnaise on hamburgers are guilty of blasphemy. My favorite combination of pizza toppings is bacon, pineapple, and jalape\u00f1o. This combination works best if you get the ratios right: more bacon than pineapple, more pineapple than jalape\u00f1o. I also am in the habit of matching meals/snacks to whatever I'm watching/eating; Pizza when watching Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles, ramen noodles while watching anime(especially Naruto), chimichangas(or any Mexican food, really) with Deadpool, lemon cakes with Game of Thrones, Oreo cookies with anything that involves Martian Manhunter and/or Miss Martian, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T16:15:00-08:00","id":1054980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1054924-what-s-your-weird-food-related-habit?p=1054974#post1054974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I liked sour cream on my French Fries.</div> </div> </div> </div>Related, is blue cheese dressing and fries a thing? Because when I was a Mini Hayley growing up in Miami, I had two really good friends, and our moms used to take us to Miami Subs to play. We used to fantasy play the Jewel Princess children's books, and one day, I don't remember how it happened, we tried the Miami Subs fries with blue cheese dressing, and then it became like a ritual. That's the impact of that story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T16:24:00-08:00","id":1054984,"title":"","content":"Oh, I used to hate egg yolk. My dad and I were regulars at a local Jewish delli and I refused to order egg whites, even when our waitress offered. For some reason I just didn't think they tasted as good if the yolk wasn't cooked with it - I just didn't want to actually <i>eat</i> the yolk. Also, I ordered them over-easy, so breakfast was always a challenge of trying to carefully cut around the yolk without breaking it and contaminating everything on my plate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T16:26:13-08:00","id":1054987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1054924-what-s-your-weird-food-related-habit?p=1054984#post1054984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I used to hate egg yolk. My dad and I were regulars at a local Jewish delli and I refused to order egg whites, even when our waitress offered. For some reason I just didn't think they tasted as good if the yolk wasn't cooked with it - I just didn't want to actually <i>eat</i> the yolk. Also, I ordered them over-easy, so breakfast was always a challenge of trying to eat as much of the whites as I could without breaking the yolk and contaminating everything on my plate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please tell me you've since learned the error of your ways! A runny egg is perhaps the greatest burger topping, and forms a holy trinity with avocado and bacon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T16:30:56-08:00","id":1054988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1054924-what-s-your-weird-food-related-habit?p=1054966#post1054966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're talking to the gal who used to suck up and spit out the pimento because she hated it, then would go to town on the now-empty olives and maybe have a sip or two of brine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Clearly, we should have been friends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T16:32:18-08:00","id":1054989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1054924-what-s-your-weird-food-related-habit?p=1054987#post1054987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please tell me you've since learned the error of your ways! A runny egg is perhaps the greatest burger topping, and forms a holy trinity with avocado and bacon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have, indeed. I enjoy the whole egg now <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It was mostly a negative association thing, as the first time I ever had a hard-boiled egg as a very small child I bit right into it not knowing it was <i>supposed</i> to have a different colored, different textured core, and assumed it was rotten. I quickly learned that was normal, but the damage had been done and for many years I just couldn't enjoy egg yolk in any form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 02-25-2017, 07:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T16:39:35-08:00","id":1054992,"title":"","content":"Not a habit per se, but I think mayonnaise is fucking abhorrent and its creation, ownership, and use would be criminal acts should I ever come to power.<br /> <br /> Eugh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T18:43:31-08:00","id":1055026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1054924-what-s-your-weird-food-related-habit?p=1054992#post1054992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not a habit per se, but I think mayonnaise is fucking abhorrent and its creation, ownership, and use would be criminal acts should I ever come to power.<br /> <br /> Eugh.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like putting mayo on a hamburger and then topping it with a handful of crunched up salt and vinegar potato chips. Makes for good contrasting texture and flavor. Does anybody else like putting potato chips on hamburgers? I often get strange looks when I do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T18:47:09-08:00","id":1055028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1054924-what-s-your-weird-food-related-habit?p=1055026#post1055026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like putting mayo on a hamburger and then topping it with a handful of crunched up salt and vinegar potato chips. Makes for good contrasting texture and flavor. Does anybody else like putting potato chips on hamburgers? I often get strange looks when I do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not something I do, but I get how it would be appealing. I like some tortilla chips in a burrito, so similar concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T22:57:17-08:00","id":1055099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1054924-what-s-your-weird-food-related-habit?p=1054992#post1054992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not a habit per se, but I think mayonnaise is fucking abhorrent and its creation, ownership, and use would be criminal acts should I ever come to power.<br /> <br /> Eugh.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mayonnaise is a crime against chemistry, nature, and good taste. Also, mushrooms are NOT food; they are what happens when food goes bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":6138,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","user":"Mangle77","date":". 02-26-2017, 02:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T23:24:22-08:00","id":1055104,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure if some of these count as weird, so I'll share the whole lot:<br /> <br /> 1) Kosher dill pickles are my favorite snack. I like them so much I have to remind myself not to eat an entire gallon-size jar in one sitting.<br /> 2) I put really hot hot sauce on the majority of my food (basically anything that isn't counter-spicy because of milk content, and also isn't normally spicy without adding sauce) because if it isn't authentic Thai food levels of spicy, I'm not completely happy eating it.<br /> 3) When I go to Wendy's for a burger, I dip my fries in a chocolate frosty if I get fries at all.<br /> 4) I will put pretty much anything that someone might make a sandwich or dip out of in a tortilla, roll it up, and eat it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not so noble anymore.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1823-drake","name":"Drake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1823_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"456"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T09:16:55-08:00","id":1055273,"title":"","content":"I always eat the ice at the bottom of the glass when I finish a drink. <br /> <br /> Just the other day I got a craving for limberger and head cheese on saltine crackers. It's something I used to eat at my grandparents as a kid, and I've been eating it all weekend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T09:36:22-08:00","id":1055284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drake</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1054924-what-s-your-weird-food-related-habit?p=1055104#post1055104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) When I go to Wendy's for a burger, I dip my fries in a chocolate frosty if I get fries at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a friend who does this. Worse he likes dipping his chicken nuggets in the frosty. I simply don't understand the appeal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T10:29:47-08:00","id":1055305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1054924-what-s-your-weird-food-related-habit?p=1055284#post1055284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have a friend who does this. Worse he likes dipping his chicken nuggets in the frosty. I simply don't understand the appeal.</div> </div> </div> </div>A little salt with an otherwise sweet thing makes it better for me because I'm not much of a fan of sweet tastes (I was that &quot;weird kid&quot; that didn't want any cake and ice cream at birthday parties, and would rather have a bologna sandwich than a candy bar as a snack). I'm not really into the combination of chocolate and chicken, so I've never gone for the nugget dipping, but it could be the same reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not so noble anymore.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1823-drake","name":"Drake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1823_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"456"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T10:39:01-08:00","id":1055307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1054924-what-s-your-weird-food-related-habit?p=1055273#post1055273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always eat the ice at the bottom of the glass when I finish a drink.<br /> <br /> Just the other day I got a craving for limberger and head cheese on saltine crackers. It's something I used to eat at my grandparents as a kid, and I've been eating it all weekend.</div> </div> </div> </div>I used to love cream cheese on saltines. Now, it's just cloyingly sweet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T10:45:04-08:00","id":1055308,"title":"","content":"How can any of you stand to crunch ice? A childhood spent in the orthodontist's chair have left my teeth hideously sensitive; the though of ice crunching is enough to make my eyes tear up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T10:54:35-08:00","id":1055312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1054924-what-s-your-weird-food-related-habit?p=1055308#post1055308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How can any of you stand to crunch ice? A childhood spent in the orthodontist's chair have left my teeth hideously sensitive; the though of ice crunching is enough to make my eyes tear up.</div> </div> </div> </div>My teeth aren't terribly sensitive to cold, and the feel of it crunching is extremely satisfying. Without the pain from the cold, it's a little like crunching a hard candy, but with a little more give so it doesn't strain your jaw, without all the sugar, and when you crush it up into small enough pieces they melt into refreshingly cool water.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T13:07:57-08:00","id":1055359,"title":"","content":"I've eaten essentially the same sandwich for lunch every workday for the last five years. A couple slices of each flavor of the club sandwich pack at BJ's, provolone cheese, oatnut bread, mustard and mayo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T15:21:42-08:00","id":1055410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1054924-what-s-your-weird-food-related-habit?p=1055359#post1055359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've eaten essentially the same sandwich for lunch every workday for the last five years.</div> </div> </div> </div>I completely forgot to mention that I used to eat the same 3 meals every day of the week for a couple years straight. Can't really remember how long because my memory and linear chronology don't really cooperate all that well - but it started with the end of my first serious relationship, and carried through until I moved to Louisiana (where there were too many amazing and new options for food to resist trying out), and was accompanied by wearing the same outfit every day (I owned 5 identical sets of clothing, and nothing else).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not so noble anymore.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1823-drake","name":"Drake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1823_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"456"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T18:35:06-08:00","id":1055492,"title":"","content":"I genuinely enjoy Spam. Eat it fairly frequently and have for a long time. I can prepare it in a variety of different ways. My favorite of late has been Spam curry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T02:16:27-08:00","id":1055571,"title":"","content":"I put honey in almost anything I cook and the milk of my pancakes is diluted with rum. I also like to add cinnamon in my salted dishes and various spices including coriander and cumin in my desserts. Lets just say that my friends prefer to ask what they are eating after they have <span style=\"color:#3C3C3C\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">c</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#303030\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">le</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#242424\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">aned their plates.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/822-daemonchrno","name":"DaemonChrno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar822_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T13:26:18-08:00","id":1056766,"title":"","content":"Hmm, lots have already been said but lets see:<br /> <br /> 1. I love mayo, its my number one go to for frys. Belgian style <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> 2. I also enjoy crunching ice, and any hard candy or cough drop or breath mint. They do not last long.<br /> 3. I add salt to chocolate milk. It just brings out the flavor so well.<br /> 4. When I eat a sit down meal I eat everything in proportion. Like I eat a third of a burger, and then a third of the fries, and a third of my drink. Then start back with the burger for another third and so on. Fast food though, is the complete opposite, I will almost always eat all of one thing before moving on to the next. All the burger, then all the fires then the drink.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T13:30:21-08:00","id":1056771,"title":"","content":"I use pickle slices as a folk remedy for mouth ulcers and cold sores.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T22:53:24-08:00","id":1060764,"title":"","content":"1. I eat fast. Under most circumstances, I am a slow moving person. Put food or drink in front of me, and most of the time, assuming that I'm not deliberately slowing myself or distractedly picking at it, said food will vanish like someone is going to steal it from me. Sometimes my wife tells me to slow down because she'll unconsciously start to match my pace and she can't eat that fast. She is also reluctant to let me hold onto any food or beverage that she knows I like, because it might not last until she gets it back.<br /> <br /> 2. I adore a good peanut butter and jelly omelette. My mom got me hooked on them when I was a kid going through my &quot;nothing but pb&amp;j phase&quot; and I've liked them ever since.<br /> <br /> 3. I, too, need to have pizza when watching anything Ninja Turtle related. It's also the time that I'm most likely to toss pretzels onto a pepperoni pizza, which is the one weird combination I actually liked during my childhood experimentations. <br /> <br /> 4. Not my own, but my nieces love ranch dressing on everything. EVERYTHING! They were spending the night, and we gave them carrots with ranch dip and a bag of fruit-flavored marshmallows for a snack. They were quite delightedly dipping the marshmallows.<br /> <br /> 5. I crunch Popsicles, especially those Pop Ice ones they have at Walmart. I can't do it with regular ice, but I have a hard time resisting with those. I also tend to check them frequently when I first put them into the freezer, because I love it when I can catch them at that middle point in the freezing where it is all solid but still soft. At that point I'll keep eating them until my wife tells me to stop.<br /> <br /> 6. Someone mentioning food tends to give me a taste for it. I'm an advertiser's dream. I can also talk with my dad for hours at a time on the subject of food.<br /> <br /> 7. I snack when running a game. I can't help it. I may have just finished dinner, but I'll still be nibbling something, no matter how full I am. If I'm truly too full, I'll still need to force myself to stop.<br /> <br /> 8. I like to play with my food. I nibble the edges of Reese's peanut butter cups, and I like to grind the filling out of the sides of an Oreo. Sometimes I even nibble the chocolate off of the outside of candy bars before devouring the delicious centers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","user":"White Oak Dragon","date":".  Apparently I can't count. I think I fixed the numbering this time. 03-10-2017, 01:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-10T00:09:45-08:00","id":1060778,"title":"","content":"Examining both sides of a Dorito chip before eating to make sure I put the side with the most flavoring on my tongue. One has to maximize their flavor coefficient after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-10T04:02:09-08:00","id":1060809,"title":"","content":"Pasta + Ketchup = Om nom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T13:12:40-07:00","id":1063416,"title":"","content":"I absolutely get the pretzel thing. I am a HUGE fan of the 'special dark splits' pretzels...oh they are so good and salty. My strange habit...and it is very strange I know is to only eat every in even bites. For example, if I am eating a taco, I have to make sure that the last bite is on an even numbered count or else I toss it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Kinda I want to&quot; - Trent Reznor<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://scontent.ftpa1-2.fna.fbcdn.net/v/t1.0-9/27973518_2040009129348529_5319855605701568493_n.jpg?oh=9c85c5c9d4a0769a1249ea2f3e62ca43&amp;oe=5B002AA5\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12143-eldritchminister","name":"EldritchMinister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12143_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T13:13:38-07:00","id":1063417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1054924-what-s-your-weird-food-related-habit?p=1060778#post1060778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Examining both sides of a Dorito chip before eating to make sure I put the side with the most flavoring on my tongue. One has to maximize their flavor coefficient after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that strange? Doesn't everyone do this?! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> This is specially great with the 'Flamas' Doritos<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Kinda I want to&quot; - Trent Reznor<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://scontent.ftpa1-2.fna.fbcdn.net/v/t1.0-9/27973518_2040009129348529_5319855605701568493_n.jpg?oh=9c85c5c9d4a0769a1249ea2f3e62ca43&amp;oe=5B002AA5\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12143-eldritchminister","name":"EldritchMinister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12143_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T13:15:11-07:00","id":1063419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1054924-what-s-your-weird-food-related-habit?p=1055308#post1055308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How can any of you stand to crunch ice? A childhood spent in the orthodontist's chair have left my teeth hideously sensitive; the though of ice crunching is enough to make my eyes tear up.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Just a FYI because my Wife does this and we found some interesting information about it... Chewing Ice, like to the point of damage to one's teeth and tongue, etc. is a sign of low iron. For years I was haunted by the sound of crunching ice everywhere in my home...then she started Iron infusions bi-weekly and viola! no more ice crunching. Believe it or not, however, she does miss it quite a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Kinda I want to&quot; - Trent Reznor<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://scontent.ftpa1-2.fna.fbcdn.net/v/t1.0-9/27973518_2040009129348529_5319855605701568493_n.jpg?oh=9c85c5c9d4a0769a1249ea2f3e62ca43&amp;oe=5B002AA5\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12143-eldritchminister","name":"EldritchMinister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12143_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T13:56:51-07:00","id":1063476,"title":"","content":"Oh, I just figured out another food habit I have that I didn't even realize until just a little while ago when my friend commented on it.<br /> <br /> When I go to Taco Bell and get a bean burrito, instead of just eating it, I'll take a bite and proceed to suck/squeeze all the beans out of the burrito, almost like it's a bagged drink, and then eat the tortilla afterwards.<br /> <br /> I did that today and when I was done my friend looked at me and said, &quot;I've seen you doing that for years and just finally have to say something about it. Are you some kind of Burrito Vampire? I always had you pegged for a Nosferatu because you're one ugly mother... but seriously that's just weird.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T15:31:52-07:00","id":1063578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1054924-what-s-your-weird-food-related-habit?p=1063476#post1063476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I just figured out another food habit I have that I didn't even realize until just a little while ago when my friend commented on it.<br /> <br /> When I go to Taco Bell and get a bean burrito, instead of just eating it, I'll take a bite and proceed to suck/squeeze all the beans out of the burrito, almost like it's a bagged drink, and then eat the tortilla afterwards.<br /> <br /> I did that today and when I was done my friend looked at me and said, &quot;I've seen you doing that for years and just finally have to say something about it. Are you some kind of Burrito Vampire? I always had you pegged for a Nosferatu because you're one ugly mother... but seriously that's just weird.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's terrible!<br /> <br /> *clearly* that's a more Malkavian trait.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}